window.docContents[228].resolve({"/Gamma-Function/___5___13-Integrals/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Gamma-Function--___5___13-Integrals--___5___13_LPAR_i_RPAR_-Barnes___-Beta-Integral":{"contents":"\\frac{1}{2\\pi}\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty}\n\\Gamma(a+it)\\Gamma(b+it)\\Gamma(c-it)\\Gamma(d-it)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n=\\frac{\\Gamma(a+c)\\Gamma(a+d)\\Gamma(b+c)\\Gamma(b+d)}\n{\\Gamma(a+b+c+d)},\\qquad\n\\Re a,\\Re b,\\Re c,\\Re d>0.All four parameters may be complex.  Positivity of each real part is the source\ncondition; under it the product of four Gamma factors is ordinarily integrable on the\nreal line, and the displayed quotient is exactly the normalized Barnes beta value.\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Gamma Function\u0009§5.13 Integrals","header":"§5.13(i) Barnes' Beta Integral","id":"/Gamma-Function/___5___13-Integrals/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Gamma-Function--___5___13-Integrals--___5___13_LPAR_i_RPAR_-Barnes___-Beta-Integral"}});